.TH CSTRING_SET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_set \- replace the entire content with a new C string
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

ccol_retval_t cstring_set(cstr s, const char *str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes the current content of s. It then puts a copy of str there. The
function grows the buffer when this is necessary. It never shrinks the
buffer.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s     String to change
str   New content (must not be NULL)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success              - Set succeeded
ccol_invalid_args         - str is NULL
ccol_container_full       - str is too large to represent. No real
                            program reaches this code. Such a str needs
                            the whole address space
ccol_not_enough_memory    - Reallocation failed
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_reset (3),
.BR cstring_append (3)
